### Keep pinned access keys stable when recents come first

**Severity:** `medium`

When recent commands are configured before pinned commands, `result.Count` assigns pinned shortcuts after the recent items. This makes Alt+1 through Alt+9 change with recent history and can leave pinned items without an access key. Allocate pinned indexes from pinned order and recent indexes from the remaining range, independently of visual section order.

```suggestion
        void AppendPinned(bool startsNewSection)
        {
            for (var i = 0; i < pinnedCount; i++)
            {
                result.Add(new ResolvedItem<T>(pinnedItems[i], true, i, startsNewSection && i == 0));
            }
        }

        void AppendRecent(bool startsNewSection)
        {
            for (var i = 0; i < recentCount; i++)
            {
                result.Add(new ResolvedItem<T>(recentItems[i], false, pinnedCount + i, startsNewSection && i == 0));
            }
        }
```
